## Caching

Caching stores previously calculated results so they can be reused.

Example:

    from functools import cache

    @cache
    def fibonacci(n):
        if n <= 1:
            return n

        return fibonacci(n - 1) + fibonacci(n - 2)

Without caching, Fibonacci repeatedly calculates the same values.

With caching:

    fibonacci(10)

stores previous results and reuses them.

Other caching techniques include:

    - functools.cache
    - functools.lru_cache
    - Application-level caches
    - Database caches
    - HTTP caches

Caching can greatly improve performance, but uses memory and can create stale-data problems.

