## Efficient Data Structures

Choosing the correct data structure can have a huge performance impact.

Common choices:

    list
        Fast indexing
        Good general-purpose sequence

    set
        Fast membership testing
        Removes duplicates

    dict
        Fast key-based lookup

    deque
        Efficient operations at both ends

    heap
        Efficient priority queue operations

Example:

    # Potentially slow
    if username in usernames_list:
        ...

    # Usually much faster for repeated membership checks
    usernames = set(usernames_list)

    if username in usernames:
        ...

The best data structure depends on what operations your program performs most often.

