## CPU-bound vs I/O-bound

This distinction is extremely important when choosing how to improve performance.

CPU-bound:

    The program spends most of its time doing calculations.

Examples:

    - Image processing
    - Mathematical calculations
    - Compression
    - Large simulations

I/O-bound:

    The program spends most of its time waiting for external operations.

Examples:

    - Network requests
    - Reading files
    - Database queries
    - API requests

CPU-bound problems often benefit from:

    - Better algorithms
    - Multiprocessing
    - Native code
    - Vectorisation

I/O-bound problems often benefit from:

    - Asyncio
    - Threads
    - Connection pooling
    - Caching
    - Batching requests

